  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The output in a factory increases according to the equation $P=P_0e^{kt}$ where $t$ is years.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $P_0$ if the initial output is 5000 units.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P_0=5000$ units.",
          "worked": "At $t=0$, $P=5000$:\n$$\\begin{align*}5000&=P_0e^0\\\\P_0&=5000\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The factory produces 8000 units after 3 years. Find the value of $k$, to 3 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k\\approx0.157$.\n\nSubstitute $8000=5000e^{3k}$ and take natural logarithms; retain $k=\\frac13\\ln(\\frac{8}{5})$ for subsequent parts.",
          "worked": "At $t=3$, $P=8000$:\n$$\\begin{align*}8000&=5000e^{3k}\\\\e^{3k}&=\\frac85\\\\3k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac85\\right)\\\\k&=\\frac13\\ln\\left(\\frac85\\right)\\\\k&\\approx0.157\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "How many units will the factory produce after 6 years?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12800$ units.",
          "worked": "Using the exact value $k=\\dfrac13\\ln\\left(\\dfrac85\\right)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(6)&=5000e^{6k}\\\\P(6)&=5000e^{2\\ln(8/5)}\\\\P(6)&=5000\\left(\\frac85\\right)^2\\\\P(6)&=12800\\text{ units}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "The factory needs to produce 20000 units to make a maximum profit.\n\nAfter how many years, correct to 1 decimal place, will this happen?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$8.8$ years.\n\nSet $20000=5000e^{kt}$ and solve $t=\\frac{\\ln(4)}{k}$ using the exact growth constant.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}20000&=5000e^{kt}\\\\e^{kt}&=4\\\\kt&=\\ln4\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln4}{k}\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln4}{\\frac13\\ln(8/5)}\\\\t&\\approx8.8\\text{ years}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
